oodle that originated in  japanese cuisine made with konjac root  and contains  97 water and 3 fiber the miracle noodle  rice and noodles have only 5 calories  per serving no fat sugar or starch and  can be used as a substitute in  traditional pasta and rice dishes  for this recipe add arugula cherry  tomatoes red onion  avocado and bacon bits to a large mixing  bowl then add your shirataki noodles  olive oil lemon juice and salt and  pepper toss to combine and add to your  jars  finally i have a beverage with benefits  that's portable and perfect for your  picnic  poppy is a bubbly drink made with apple  cider vinegar and prebiotics which are a  type  of fiber that helps selectively nourish  the good bacteria in the gut which helps  support a healthy immune system  unlike traditional soda it's low in  calories and sugar but still comes in  delicious flavors like ginger lime  watermelon and my favorite the  strawberry lemon  i hope you enjoyed these tips and  recipes you can find them at my website  nutritionbymia.com and nutritionbymia on  instagram where i also share meal ideas  and nutrition tips daily
 

